{"step_index":81,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T12:58:37Z","thinking":"**Designing Medicine Verification Logic**\n\nPlan is to create a JavaScript file for client-side medicine verification, fetching data via an API endpoint. This verification system requires supporting both manual search inputs and barcode simulation. The UI will then render a Verification Result Card displaying key medicine details based on the API response. The card will dynamically display a header indicating the verification status: \"Database Match\", \"Needs Review\", \"Alert\", or \"Not Found.\" Furthermore, the UI will showcase medicine details such as brand name, generic name, manufacturer, dosage form, strength, registration number and price, in addition to the batch number and its manufacturing date and expiry.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"/**\\n * MedCheck BD - Verification Client Script\\n * Handles live medicine & batch verification lookups, barcode simulation, and UI rendering.\\n */\\n\\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {\\n  const urlParams = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search);\\n  const initialQuery = urlParams.get('query');\\n  if (initialQuery) {\\n    const input = document.getElementById('verifyInput');\\n    if (input) input.value = decodeURIComponent(initialQuery);\\n    executeVerification(initialQuery);\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// Barcode simulation: sets demo barcode into search field\\nfunction simulateBarcodeScan(barcode = '894110000101') {\\n  const input = document.getElementById('verifyInput');\\n  if (!input) return;\\n  input.value = barcode;\\n  showToast(`Scanned Barcode: ${barcode}`, 'info');\\n  executeVerification(barcode);\\n}\\n\\n// Main verification handler\\nasync function handleVerifySubmit(e) {\\n  if (e) e.preventDefault();\\n  const input = document.getElementById('verifyInput');\\n  const query = input ? input.value.trim() : '';\\n\\n  if